While I'm at it, I think I'll post my (unabridged) Wish list.
It's rather long, so you might want to skip the rest of this article.

weapons:
(Lawful or Chaotic) blessed +2 longsword named Frost Brand
	reason: by use of a helm of opposite alignment, it is possible for
		a Lawful character to get Chaotic weapons, a Chaotic 
		character to get Lawful weapons, and a Neutral character to
		get all artifacts.  It isn't possible for a L or C character
		to get Neutral weapons, though.

(Neutral) blessed +2 broadsword named Stormbringer
	reason: simply one of the two best weapons, the other (Excalibur)
		can be had in other, easier ways.

armor:
blessed +2 gray dragon scale mail
	reason: the best body armor to be had, dragon scale mail adds 9
		to your AC before the plus.  Gray dragon scale mail gives
		the wearer resistance to magic which, unlike all the other
		forms of dragon scale, cannot be gained by eating the 
		dragon's corpse.  It can be had by a cloak, but this allows
		the wearer to wear a different cloak and still have magic
		protection.

blessed +2 helm of telepathy
	reason: although telepathy can be gained by eating floating eyes,
		I find that the ability to see through walls is invaluable.
		A helm of brilliance would be nice for spellcasters, but I
		find that even when I play one I don't cast spells often
		enough to make it worthwhile.  A helm of opposite alignment,
		while handy for procuring artifacts and praying in hell, is
		simply not useful enough to be wished for.

blessed +2 gauntlets of dexterity
	reason: although gauntlets of power are handy for low level characters,
		once a character has strength 18/** (under the easy option)
		or over 18 (under the HARD option), they become superfluous.
		Gauntlets of dexterity, on the other hand, always augment
		the wearer's abilities, even if he has 18 dex without them.

blessed +2 boots of speed
	reason: simply the most useful boots to be had.

(for characters without intrinsic stealth)
blessed +2 elven cloak
	reason: stealth is a much more important ability than protection
		or displacement.  Invisibility can be gained without the
		use of a cloak or rings (though I wouldn't advise this until
		you have an alternate method of entering shops), and magic
		resistance can be had via body armor (see above)

(for characters with intrinsic stealth)
blessed +2 cloak of protection
	reason: displacement isn't particularly useful if you already have
		intrinsic invisibility.  see also the previous paragraph.

blessed +2 shield of reflection
	reason: It's the only shield that gives any extra abilities, plus
		it lowers your AC by 2 before the plus and is naturally
		rust-proof.

amulets:
blessed amulet of life saving
	reason: there's no better proof against stupid deaths.

food:
3 blessed tins of whatever-monster-gives-me-an-intrinsic-I-don't-already-have
	-or-
3 blessed tins of wraith meat
	reason: the first should be self-explanatory.
		the second, even though you can't tin wraiths, tins of
		wraith meat can be wished for and they automatically
		raise you one level each time you eat one.

potions:
3 blessed potions of gain ability

3 potions of gain level (blessed or uncursed makes little difference)
	reason: should be obvious

scrolls:
3 blessed scrolls of enchant [weapon, armor]

3 blessed scrolls of remove curse
	reason: I always seem to have something that needs un-cursing.

3 blessed scrolls of genocide

3 cursed scrolls of genocide
	reason: Good for summoning large numbers of Wraiths, Nurses, or
		some monster that will give me an intrinsic I don't yet have.

gems & stones:
a blessed luckstone
	reason: blessed luckstones only affect your luck if it is positive.
		uncursed luckstones maintain your luck at its current level
		regardless if it is good or bad.

tools:
a blessed blindfold (if I don't already have one)

a blessed magic marker
	reason: for making blessed scrolls.

a blessed tinning kit
	reason: for making blessed tins, in case I lose an intrinsic.
		(If I get hungry, I'll eat the corpse)

a blessed stethoscope

rings:
a blessed ring of conflict

a blessed ring of levitation

a blessed +5 ring of protection
	reason: I don't use polymorph that much.

wands:
a blessed wand of polymorph
	reason: I *do* use the poly-pile trick, however.

spellbooks:
a blessed spellbook of knock
	reason: so I don't have to play the master-mind game when I get
		to the castle

	(I don't tend to cast spells very often.)

...that usually exhausts my wishing ability.

Note that wishing for magic lamps and wands of wishing is pointless,
since the wands will always have -1 charges and the lamps will always
have 0 charges.  If you have a blessed scroll of charging, better to use
it on the item you were using to make the wish in the first place.

